(How Retrieval-Augmented Generation Works) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Retrieval-augmented generation, or RAG, answers questions using a set of documents.) Tj T*
(A language model on its own answers from what it learned during training, so it can) Tj T*
(be out of date and knows nothing about your private files. RAG adds a search step:) Tj T*
(it finds passages related to the question and gives them to the model as context.) Tj T*
(The model is then asked to answer from those passages.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The approach has two phases. Indexing prepares the documents once, ahead of time.) Tj T*
(Querying runs each time someone asks a question.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
