(Indexing: Preparing Documents) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Indexing begins by extracting the text of each document. Long text is then split into) Tj T*
(smaller chunks, because a search works best when each result covers one idea.) Tj T*
(Overlap between neighbouring chunks keeps a sentence that crosses a boundary whole.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An embedding model converts each chunk into a vector, a list of numbers that captures) Tj T*
(its meaning. Chunks with similar meanings get vectors that are close together. The) Tj T*
(vectors are stored in a vector index, which can find the nearest ones quickly. Saving) Tj T*
(the index means the slow embedding work doesn't have to be repeated at every start.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
